### P02768 – Human Serum Albumin (ALB)

P02768 corresponds to Human Serum Albumin (ALB), the most abundant protein in human blood plasma. It plays a crucial role in maintaining 
osmotic pressure and transporting hormones, fatty acids, drugs, and other molecules throughout the body. Due to its well-characterized 
structure and biological significance, it is widely used in bioinformatics studies for protein characterization and physicochemical
property analysis.
